        "question_id": "q-127083",
        "problem": "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{′}(x)\\,=\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
        "status": "ambiguous",
        "answers": [
          {
            "key": "field-1",
            "correct_value": "-6x^{2}+12x+18",
            "ma_basis": "none"
          }
        ],
        "feedback": {
          "grade": "Correct",
          "result": "Correct",
          "worked_solution": "We differentiate the function, applying the addition, constant multiple, and power rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+18x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2{x}^{3})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(18x) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})+6\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+18\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 3{x}^{(3-1)}+6\\cdot 2{x}^{(2-1)}+18\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-6{x}^{2}+12x+18\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14285419/observations/step-2-fed7b648b8828ae09817.html"
